# Every text file in this repository is LF, in the working tree as well as in
# the object store.
#
# This is not a style preference. build.py copies shared/ and each tool's src/
# into dist/ byte for byte, so if a checkout on Windows had CRLF and a checkout
# in CI had LF, the same sources would produce two different sites and
# `python build.py --check` would report a difference that is not really there.
# The whole point of that command is that a reader can prove the deployed site
# is a build of these sources, so the build has to be reproducible on any
# machine.
#
# Files build.py writes itself are already forced to LF in code; this covers
# the ones it only copies.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so Git must not touch them at all.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
